# KIDDO — environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development (gitignored). On Netlify, set
# the same names under Site configuration → Environment variables.
#
# Every variable here is optional. Without the Firebase ones KIDDO runs in
# device-only mode: no accounts, progress in localStorage, exactly as before
# Phase 8B. With Firebase but without the server-side block below, parents
# can sign in but the subscription gate answers "billing is not set up"
# (HTTP 503) and no one gets through it.
#
# Two kinds of value live here. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are compiled into the
# browser bundle and are identifiers, not secrets (a Firebase web API key
# grants nothing by itself; access is enforced by firestore.rules). The
# values WITHOUT that prefix are secrets: they are read only by the route
# handlers under src/app/api and must never be renamed to NEXT_PUBLIC_*.

# Production origin, used for canonical URLs and og:image (Phase 7).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Meta (Facebook) pixel. Digits only — the dataset id from Meta Events
# Manager → Datasets. Set it on the production site only: any other build
# would report its page views — and its test purchases — into the same
# dataset, and on Netlify a variable applies to every deploy context unless
# it is scoped. Loaded on the parent-facing pages alone (/, /join,
# /welcome, /privacy, /parents); a child's screen never contacts Facebook.
# Page views, plus InitiateCheckout and Purchase with the plan and its
# price (src/lib/analytics/events.ts). Leave empty and no page reports.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# Firebase web app config for project kiddocares-b105e.
# Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps → Web app → SDK setup.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# The host Firebase serves /__/auth/handler from, and so the host Google's
# account chooser shows the parent. In production it is KIDDO's own domain:
# netlify.toml proxies /__/auth/* through to Firebase Hosting, so the handler
# is same-origin with the page that opened it — which is what lets an
# installed iPhone sign in by redirect at all (src/lib/firebase/config.ts).
# Leave it empty locally and it falls back to the project's own
# kiddocares-b105e.firebaseapp.com, where the popup every other browser uses
# works unchanged.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=kiddocares.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=kiddocares-b105e
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ---- Server-only secrets (Phase 8C). Never NEXT_PUBLIC_. ------------------

# Firebase service account for kiddocares-b105e, as the JSON file's contents
# or that JSON base64-encoded (one line). Firebase console → Project
# settings → Service accounts → Generate new private key. Lets the server
# verify ID tokens, write users/{uid}.access, and delete accounts.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=

# ---- Billplz: how KIDDO is bought. ---------------------------------------
#
# One payment of RM29.90 (the launch price; RM39.90 is only ever shown
# struck through) for lifetime access. The amount is not configured
# here — it is LIFETIME_AMOUNT in src/lib/billing/access.ts, in sen — so
# there is one number in one file and no way for an environment to disagree
# with the price on the page.
#
# BILLPLZ_SECRET_KEY is a secret. It is never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never read from
# a client component (src/server/billplz.ts is `server-only`, which makes
# that a build error rather than a leak), and never committed.

# "sandbox" (the default, and what everything below should be while you are
# testing) or "production". Anything other than the exact word "production"
# means sandbox, so a half-finished configuration takes test payments
# rather than real ones.
BILLPLZ_MODE=sandbox
# Billplz dashboard → Settings → your account → API keys → Secret Key.
# Sandbox keys come from www.billplz-sandbox.com, production keys from
# www.billplz.com; they are different accounts and different keys.
BILLPLZ_SECRET_KEY=
# The collection KIDDO's lifetime bills are created in. Billplz dashboard →
# Billing → Collections → create one ("KIDDO Lifetime Access") and copy its
# id. A bill outside this collection can never open KIDDO — the server
# checks the collection on every bill it reads.
BILLPLZ_COLLECTION_ID=
# The collection's X-Signature key, which is what proves a callback really
# came from Billplz. Billplz dashboard → Settings → your account →
# X Signature Key (enable it for the collection). Optional but strongly
# recommended: with it set, an unsigned or wrongly signed callback is
# refused outright; without it the server still believes nothing until it
# has re-read the bill from Billplz itself.
BILLPLZ_XSIGNATURE_KEY=

# ---- Stripe: the subscriptions sold before KIDDO was sold once. ----------
#
# Nothing new goes through Stripe. These are only needed so the parents who
# already subscribed keep their access, their Customer Portal and a clean
# account deletion; see docs/kiddo-billing.md. A deployment with no such
# parents can leave them empty.
# Stripe dashboard → Developers → API keys.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Stripe dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → endpoint for
# https://<site>/api/billing/webhook → Signing secret. Locally, the secret
# printed by `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/billing/webhook`.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# The two recurring prices those subscriptions were sold on. No new
# subscription is created, so these are read only to name an existing one.
STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=
STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY=

# ---- App Check (Phase 8D hardening). ------------------------------------

# reCAPTCHA Enterprise site key for App Check. Firebase console → App Check
# → Apps → register the web app. An identifier, not a secret: it is what
# lets a real browser prove it is one before calling a parent API route.
# Leave empty and App Check is simply not started, which is what local
# development and the test suite do.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_CHECK_KEY=
# "recaptcha-enterprise" (default) or "recaptcha-v3".
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_CHECK_PROVIDER=
# A debug token from Firebase console → App Check → Apps → Manage debug
# tokens, for running a real browser against an enforcing project. Never
# set this on the production site.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_CHECK_DEBUG_TOKEN=
# "true" makes the server reject parent API calls that arrive without a
# valid App Check token. Turn this on only after the key above is live and
# the Firebase console shows verified traffic; see docs/SECURITY.md.
APP_CHECK_ENFORCED=

# ---- Build-time switches. -----------------------------------------------

# "true" sends the Content-Security-Policy as report-only. Read by
# `next build`, not by `next start`, because headers() is baked into the
# build. Leave empty in production so the policy is enforced.
CSP_REPORT_ONLY=
# "1" includes the /playground and /character reference screens in the
# build. Required for `npm run measure:*`. MUST stay empty in production:
# it is what keeps those screens out of the deployed bundle entirely.
KIDDO_DEV_PAGES=
